d$ if $z =-c - d\\textrm{i}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055513 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1234cf5e-bc44-54a6-aa08-551f55b5254e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055736 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055736 #edb/ref 1061 464642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055736 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "332a5684-42f1-5051-9109-e6eecf07792c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055736 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055737 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055737 #edb/ref 1061 464643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055737 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb92b79b-ab97-5fdc-b40d-801d52bba2ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055737 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055738 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055738 #edb/ref 1061 464646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055738 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd86a525-dbf1-5d5d-8bce-6a9c5a832457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055738 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055739 #edb/ref 1061 464649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055739 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ea96e969-a594-52d8-a7bc-fe570264819e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055739 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055976 #edb/ref 1064 "The **magnitude** of a complex number is its distance from the origin. It's denoted as $\\mid z \\mid$.\n\nFor example, consider the complex number\n\n$$\nz=-4+5\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nshown in the complex plane below.\n\n![](images/33/33d0294178c15b883f8f4988e34d7c81244edd9f426e9ed206e10469dbc5abf1.png)\n\nUsing the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2} + (5)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{41}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, for a complex number\n\n$$\nz=a+b\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nthe magnitude of $z$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mid z \\mid